From 59712bab588d41cc1a5394062b90982b79a30fd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shiro <build@shiro>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 04:49:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] emscripten: wasm JIT (wjit): hot x86-64 regions become
 WebAssembly functions

Hot regions (basic blocks reachable through direct branches from a hot
branch target) are translated into wasm functions that keep guest registers
in locals, inline common integer ops, memory accesses (through a per-thread
translation cache) and fused compare+branch, and call Blink's own op
handlers for everything else. Modules import the shared memory and the C
helpers they call and are installed in the function table; the interpreter
loop calls them. Code is compiled only from non-writable pages; unmapping
or reprotecting such a page invalidates every thread's regions.
---
